StickyNote {
 inputs 0
 name StickyNote1
 label "Scene (m) -- coverage fill: the silhouette halo\n\nCheck: a defocused opaque card in front of the focal plane must keep alpha 1 across its silhouette whether or not the renderer wrote occluded samples behind it, and the coverage the node fills in must carry the FOREGROUND's colour.\n\nThe card is 96x96 at z=4 with focus at z=20 and size 4, i.e. a CoC radius of 16 px exactly; the background sits ON the focal plane, so it cannot scatter inward and any background colour inside the silhouette would be invented. FG and BG share G and B and differ only in R (FG 0.80, BG 0.20), so G/A and B/A are known analytically everywhere and R/A reads the FG:BG mix.\n\nThree branches:\n  control (m0): DeepMerge2 of card over background -- occluded samples PRESENT. Alpha 1 across the silhouette, colour ratio the source's; in the edge band the fill overshoots and the clamp brings the premultiplied pair back down together.\n  halo (m1): ONE sample per pixel, no background behind the card. Used to read alpha 0.27 at the card's corner and 0.52 at its edge (a 16 px halo); must now read 1 to within 1/255, and the filled band is FG colour (R/A 0.80).\n  card over nothing (m2): the bloom must be UNCHANGED by the fill -- pinned two-sided against the pre-fill plugin's profile across the right edge on y=128 (-1: 0.5199, 0: 0.4801, +7: 0.2130, +14: 0.0170, +16: exactly 0). This holds only because the scene is single-depth: the empty pixels' virtual background scatters at the farthest measured depth's CoC, which for one object is its own."
 note_font_size 14
 xpos 480
}
Constant {
 inputs 0
 color {0 0 0 0.5}
 format "256 256 0 0 256 256 1 deepc_val_256"
